                <mxCell id="405" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#f9a825;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" value="Templated headers (librechat.yaml):&#xa;Authorization: Bearer ${CONVERSE_OPENAI_API_KEY}&#xa;X-LibreChat-User:  {{LIBRECHAT_USER_OPENIDID}}&#xa;X-LibreChat-Role:  {{LIBRECHAT_USER_ROLE}}&#xa;X-LibreChat-Email: {{LIBRECHAT_USER_EMAIL}}&#xa;X-LibreChat-Name:  {{LIBRECHAT_USER_NAME}}" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="120" width="330" x="300" y="250" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="406" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce4ec;strokeColor=#ad1457;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;align=center;" value="Envoy AI Gateway&#xa;api-internal listener (ClusterIP only)&#xa;core-gateway-internal…:443" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="70" width="260" x="700" y="120" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="407" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce4ec;strokeColor=#ad1457;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" value="Authorino — internal AuthConfig (CEL)&#xa;1. Authenticate: apiKey Secret internal-key-librechat&#xa;   (label kuadrant.io/apikey-for=internal-gateway)&#xa;2. x-account-id = x-org-id = X-LibreChat-User&#xa;   IF present, non-empty AND not containing &quot;{{&quot;&#xa;3. x-billing-plan = (X-LibreChat-Role == &quot;pro&quot;) ? pro : free&#xa;4. x-oidc-email / x-oidc-name ← forwarded headers&#xa;5. x-api-key-id, x-quota-tier, x-model-policy = &quot;&quot;&#xa;6. dynamicMetadata budget.enforced = false&#xa;Authorino OVERWRITES these — a client cannot pick its plan" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="200" width="420" x="700" y="240" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="408" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe0b2;strokeColor=#e65100;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;align=center;" value="Lyft ratelimit (per model)&#xa;rule x-account-id × model&#xa;→ N req/min PER USER" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="80" width="200" x="700" y="490" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="409" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f5e9;strokeColor=#2e7d32;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;align=center;" value="Grafana per-user boards&#xa;(Loki/Mimir: user_id,&#xa;email, name)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="80" width="190" x="930" y="490" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="410" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#4527a0;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;align=center;" value="opencode (external plane)&#xa;same person → same&#xa;x-account-id (Keycloak/authz sub)" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="80" width="230" x="300" y="490" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="411" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=6;" value="Why trusting a header is OK here:&#xa;• the internal listener is ClusterIP-only and accepts only authenticated first-party services&#xa;• Authorino rewrites the descriptors on every request&#xa;Why the &quot;{{&quot; guard: 2026-08-01 a paid request arrived with account_id literally &quot;{{LIBRECHAT_USER_OPENIDID}}&quot;&#xa;— without the guard, every such request would pool into one fake account.&#xa;Note: LibreChat roles are USER/ADMIN, so LibreChat users land on the &quot;free&quot; plan in practice." vertex="1">
